re available?\n\n2 configuration(s), including 4 BHK of 3919 sqft at ₹59 Cr. See the pricing table above.\n\nWho is the developer?\n\nBirla Estates — 4 projects tracked on Mumbai Property Exchange.\n\nHow do I book or get more details?\n\nTap WhatsApp or Call below to speak with a Mumbai Property Exchange advisor — serving Mumbai since 1995 · RERA-registered since 2017.\n\nSOURCE · MAHARERA + MUMBAI PROPERTY EXCHANGE  \nINDEPENDENT DATA · RERA A51800043517 · EST. 1995\n\n[WhatsApp](https://wa.me/919820067525?text=I%20am%20looking%20to%20buy%20a%20home%20in%20Project%20Birla%20Anayu%20(RERA%20P51900077140))[Enquire ▸](https://wa.me/919820067525?text=I%20am%20looking%20to%20buy%20a%20home%20in%20Project%20Birla%20Anayu%20(RERA%20P51900077140))\n\n🎯 AI Matchmaker\n\nTell us what you want in Malabar Hill — get matched\n\nRERA-verified options on WhatsApp. No spam, no fakes.\n\n[New launch\n\nAkshar Elevate, Vashi\n\nNew launch in Vashi — ₹28,895/sq.ft\n\nView project ›](/ad-click/900045)\n\n## 📰 Latest Mumbai Property News\n\n[View all news →](/news)\n\n[![Dhuleva Plans ₹1,000 Crore Redevelopment Near Marine Lines](https://www.mumbaipropertyexchange.com/img/news/8ab151e7dd57.png)\n\nArticles\n\nDhuleva Plans ₹1,000 Crore Redevelopment Near Marine Lines\n\n📅 28 Sep 2026](/news/2001893/dhuleva-plans-1-000-crore-redevelopment-near-marine-lines)[![Mumbai MMR Targets $1.5 Trillion Economy by 2047](https://www.mumbaipropertyexchange.com/img/news/1db71ca6a520.jpg)\n\nArticles\n\nMumbai MMR Targets $1.5 Trillion Economy by 2047\n\n📅 04 Sep 2026](/news/2001923/mumbai-mmr-targets-1-5-trillion-economy-by-2047)[![HC Clears Development of 48-Acre Swadeshi Mills Land in Mumbai](https://www.mumbaipropertyexchange.com/img/news/0445cfc31f2f.jpg)\n\nArticles\n\nHC Clears Development of 48-Acre Swadeshi Mills Land in Mumbai\n\n📅 04 Sep 2026](/news/2001910/hc-clears-development-of-48-acre-swadeshi-mills-land-in-mumbai)[![Kamdhenu Realities Buys 4-Acre Navi Mumbai Land for ₹150 Crore](https://www.mumbaipropertyexchange.com/img/news/06ac4371a40f.jpg)\n\nArticles\n\nKamdhenu Realities Buys 4-Acre Navi Mumbai Land for ₹150 Crore\n\n📅 01 Sep 2026](/news/2001905/kamdhenu-realities-buys-4-acre-navi-mumbai-land-for-150-crore)","images":[]},{"url":"https://realtypromoo.com/projects/birla-khar-west","title":"Birla Khar West Mumbai — Pre-Launch Price & Review","raw_content":"[Realty**Promoo**™](/)\n\n\n\n![Birla Khar West — 3 BHK — Khar West — Mumbai](/images/projects/birla-khar-west-3.webp \"Birla Khar West\")\n\nPhoto by Randomclicks via Google Places\n\n# Birla Khar West\n\nℹ️ **RERA registration in progress.** Pricing and configurations shown are indicative and may change upon final RERA approval.\n\nBy The RealtyPromoo Research Team\n\n[Birla Estates Private Limited](/developers/birla-estates-private-limited)\n\n[Khar West](/mumbai/khar-west)\n\nPrice on Request\n\n3 BHK\n\nProject Scorecard by RealtyPromoo\n\n4.0 / 5\n\n★★★★⯨  4.7\n\nConstruction Quality\n\n★★★⯨★  3.5\n\n★★★★★  4.0\n\nValue for Money\n\n★★★⯨★  3.6\n\nBuilder Reputation\n\n★★★★★  4.2\n\n## About Birla [Khar West](/mumbai/khar-west)\n\nBirla Khar West is a forthcoming ultra-luxury residential redevelopment project announced by Birla Estates (a wholly-owned subsidiary of Aditya Birla Real Estate Limited) in March 2026. The project involves the redevelopment of two co-operative housing societies — Anmol Co-operative Housing Society and Bhartiya Bhavan Co-operative Housing Society — in Khar West, [Mumbai](/cities/mumbai)'s western suburbs. Developed as a joint venture with Parinee Real Estate Builders, it spans approximately 1.3 acres with a total saleable area of 2.9 lakh sq.ft. The development will deliver luxury residential apartments with an estimated revenue potential of ₹1,700 crore. This is Birla Estates' first-ever redevelopment project in the Mumbai Metropolitan Region.\n\n## Key Highlights\n\n* **1.3-acre redevelopment site** unlocking 2.9 lakh sq.ft of saleable area — compact but high-value in a land-scarce micro-market\n* **Revenue potential of ₹1,700 crore**, implying an average realisation of ~₹58,600/sq.ft based on current market analysis\n* **Joint venture with Parinee Real Estate Builders** — Birla Estates brings brand capital and design DNA; Parinee brings local Mumbai redevelopment expertise\n* **3 BHK apartments of ~1,906 sq.ft** (Super Built-Up) per broker channel materials; 74 residential units with fully air-conditioned layouts\n* **20 high-street retail units** planned within the development, adding daily convenience and commercial value to the address\n* **0.6 km from the upcoming Khar Metro Station** (Metro Line 2, Dahisar–Mankhurd) and ~1.3 km from Khar Road Railway Station on the Western line\n* **Birla Estates' MMR debut in redevelopment** — the company already runs [Birla Niyaara](/projects/birla-niyaara) ([Worli](/mumbai/worli)) and has Grade-A commercial assets in Mumbai, giving it a proven Mumbai execution base\n* **Rooftop sky lounge, swimming pool, gym, yoga studio** and a rooftop running track indicated in broker materials — full amenity list subject to RERA filing\n\n## Location Advantages\n\nKhar West sits between Bandra and Santacruz in Mumbai's western suburbs — arguably one of the city's most well-established premium residential pockets. Khar Road Railway Station is under 1 km away, connecting to Bandra in 5 minutes and Andheri in roughly 10 minutes by local train. Bandra–[Kurla](/mumbai/kurla) Complex (BKC), one of Mumbai's largest commercial districts, is approximately 6 km out — a 15–20 minute drive in normal traffic. The Mumbai International Airport is approximately 8.5 km away (roughly 20–25 minutes off-peak).\n\nThe Bandra–Worli Sea Link, accessible in about 5 km south, gives fast access to Lower [Parel](/mumbai/parel) and South Mumbai on weekday mornings. Linking Road — arguably Mumbai's most vibrant shopping street — is within easy walking or auto-rickshaw distance.\n\n**Honest concern:** Ongoing metro construction work (Metro Line 2) has caused dust, traffic diversions, and noise in parts of Khar West — a real near-term lifestyle issue. Internal roads can face congestion during school hours. Parking in this micro-market is perennially tight. Once the metro is operational, however, connectivity will meaningfully improve.\n\n## What's Nearby — Schools, Hospitals, Malls\n\n| Category | Name | Distance | Drive Time |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| School (CBSE) | R.N. Podar School, [Santacruz West](/mumbai/santacruz-west) | ~1.5 km | 5–7 min |\n| School (IB/Cambridge) | Podar International School, Santacruz | ~2 km | 7–10 min |\n| School (ICSE) | Beacon High School, Khar West | ~0.8 km | 3–5 min |\n| School (CBSE) | KB Patil International School, Khar | ~1.2 km | 4–6 min |\n| Hospital (Multi-Specialty) | Hinduja Healthcare, Khar | ~0.7 km | 3–5 min |\n| Hospital (Urology/Laparoscopy) | RG Stone Urology & Laparoscopy Hospital, Khar | ~0.5 km | 2–3 min |\n| Hospital (Multi-Specialty) | Ramakrishna Mission Hospital, Khar | ~1.1 km | 4–6 min |\n| Shopping / Market | Linking Road (Bandra), street retail | ~1.5 km | 5–8 min |\n| Mall | Hi-Life Mall, Malad (larger anchor) | ~12 km | 25–35 min |\n| Market / Daily Needs | Veena Beena Shopping Centre & Prabhat Chamber, Khar | ~0.6 km | 2–4 min |\n| Dining / Entertainment | Carter Road Promenade, Bandra | ~2.5 km | 8–12 min |\n| Business Hub | Bandra–Kurla Complex (BKC) | ~6 km | 15–20 min |\n\n## Amenities\n\nBased on broker channel materials circulating ahead of the formal RERA launch, Birla Khar West is expected to offer the following amenity mix. Final specifications will be confirmed at RERA registration stage.\n\n* **Fitness & Sports:** Fully equipped gymnasium, yoga and meditation studio, rooftop running track, indoor games room\n* **Water:** Swimming pool (with children's pool expected)\n* **Social:** Rooftop sky lounge, amphitheatre with landscaped garden backdrop, clubhouse with large-format windows, multi-purpose halls\n* **Kids:** Dedicated children's play area, seating plazas nestled within lush lawns\n* **Sustainability:** Rainwater harvesting systems, energy-efficient lighting throughout common areas, water-saving fixtures, eco-friendly construction materials\n* **Security:** 24/7 CCTV surveillance, gated access with visitor management systems\n* **Retail:** 20 high-street retail units at ground/podium level for daily convenience\n\nBroker materials cite over 30 amenities in total — but until RERA is filed and the approved plan is public, treat this list as indicative, not contractual.\n\n## Price & Configuration\n\nBirla Khar West is at pre-RERA stage and the developer has not officially released any pricing. Official pricing and confirmed configurations will only be disclosed at the time of RERA filing and formal launch.\n\nFor context: the Khar West micro-market averaged ₹56,663/sq.ft in Q4 2025 (up 16.4% year-on-year), while listed resale inventory currently averages ₹63,450/sq.ft. Analyst reverse-calculation of the ₹1,700 crore revenue target across 2.9 lakh sq.ft of saleable area implies an average selling price of approximately ₹58,600/sq.ft. A new-launch Birla product in this address tier is likely to be priced at or above this average.\n\n| Type | Area (Super Built-Up, sq.ft.)\\* | Indicative Price | Indicative Rate/sq.ft. |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| 3 BHK | ~1,906 sq.ft. (SBU)\\* | ₹11 Cr – ₹14 Cr (est.) | ~₹58,000–₹73,500/sq.ft. |\n\n*\\*Carpet area not confirmed at pre-RERA stage. Area labelled as Super Built-Up (SBU) from broker marketing materials only.*  \n*\\*\\*Estimated range based on area average transacted rates and revenue potential back-calculation. Not official developer pricing. Final prices will differ.*\n\nNo confirmed payment plan is available at this stage. Construction-Linked Plan (CLP) and flexi options are typical for Birla Estates projects at RERA stage.\n\n**⚠️ Price Disclaimer:** Prices shown are indicative and based on RealtyPromoo research. Actual cost may vary based on floor rise, PLC (Preferential Location Charge), parking, GST, registration and developer-specific charges. **Contact us for the latest verified cost sheet.**\n\n## Investment Analysis\n\n* **Current area average:** Khar West transacted at ₹56,663/sq.ft (Q4 2025), up from ₹48,696/sq.ft a year prior — a 16.4% YoY gain. Listed inventory averages ₹63,450/sq.ft.\n* **Price appreciation trend:** Khar West has delivered approximately 8.5% appreciation in the last 12 months and 15.4% over three years — comfortably above Mumbai's broader suburban average.\n* **Rental yield:** Current rental yield for Khar West stands at approximately 4% annually. Monthly rents for a 3 BHK in this area range from ₹1.5 lakh to ₹3 lakh depending on size and floor.\n* **Land scarcity premium:** There is virtually no new freehold land available for greenfield development in Khar West. Redevelopment projects command a scarcity premium that supports long-term capital appreciation.\n* **Metro Line 2 upside:** The upcoming Khar Metro Station at ~0.6 km is a clear medium-term value driver — similar station-proximity premiums in other Mumbai corridors have historically added 10–15% to values after operationalisation.\n* **Comparable projects:** [Rustomjee Paramount](/projects/rustomjee-paramount) (Khar West) — currently trading at ~₹74,100/sq.ft with RERA and OC; Girish Wild Teasel (Khar West) — listed at ~₹65,000/sq.ft under construction. A new Birla launch at ₹58,000–₹73,000/sq.ft would be competitive if confirmed at those levels.\n* **Risk flag:** This is Birla Estates' first redevelopment project in MMR. Redevelopment timelines in Mumbai are notoriously unpredictable — society NOC delays, regulatory approvals, and rehabilitation accommodation complexities have historically pushed timelines 12–24 months beyond original schedules even for experienced developers.\n\n## Pros and Cons\n\n### Pros\n\n* **Blue-chip micro-market:** Khar West has one of the most consistent appreciation records in Mumbai's western suburbs, with virtually zero new land supply for greenfield development.\n* **Metro connectivity imminent:** The planned Khar Metro Station at ~0.6 km will directly boost BKC and cross-harbour commute options — a structural advantage few competing projects in this locality offer.\n* **Trusted brand with Mumbai track record:** Birla Estates already operates Birla Niyaara (Worli) and commercial assets in Mumbai — this is not a developer entering Mumbai cold; they have local execution credibility.\n* **Parinee Group JV:** Parinee Real Estate brings specific Mumbai redevelopment experience, which helps de-risk the complex society-negotiation and regulatory-approval process that stalls many redevelopment projects.\n* **Low-density, premium product:** Only 74 residential units across 1.3 acres signals a low-density development — residents get exclusivity, not a high-rise colony feel.\n\n### Cons\n\n* **No RERA yet — significant risk:** As of June 2026, MahaRERA registration has not been filed. No committed possession date exists. Buyers considering pre-RERA commitments should exercise extreme caution.\n* **First redevelopment in MMR for Birla Estates:** Redevelopment projects are structurally more complex than greenfield — society consent, transit accommodation, and bureaucratic approvals introduce timeline risks that even experienced developers misjudge.\n* **Metro construction disruption:** Ongoing Metro Line 2 construction is causing dust, road diversions, and noise near Khar West — a real near-term quality-of-life issue for residents of the area.\n* **Premium pricing ceiling:** With area averages already at ₹56,000–₹63,000/sq.ft, the all-in cost (including floor rise, PLC, GST, registration) for a top-floor 3 BHK could breach ₹18–20 Cr — limiting the pool of end-user buyers and increasing reliance on investor absorption.\n\n## Who Should Buy This\n\n**Ideal for:** High-net-worth end-users who want to live in Khar West — families already working in BKC, Bandra, or with children in the area's schools will value the genuine locational merit here. NRI investors looking for a Tier-1 Mumbai address in a supply-constrained micro-market, comfortable with a 4–5 year horizon, may find this compelling. Investors who bought into Birla Niyaara at launch and benefited from that appreciation cycle may want exposure here at a lower absolute ticket size.\n\n**Not ideal for:** Buyers who need RERA protection before committing funds, those expecting possession within 2–3 years, or anyone seeking a ready-to-move or near-delivery product — this project is at least 4–5 years from possession. Budget buyers looking at sub-₹10 Cr tickets should look elsewhere in the western suburbs.\n\n## FAQ — Frequently Asked Questions\n\n**Q: Is Birla Khar West RERA registered?**\n\nA: No. As of June 2026, Birla Khar West has not received its MahaRERA registration. The developer's own marketing materials state \"RERA Number — Coming Soon.\" Do not commit funds based on pre-RERA broker marketing alone.\n\n**Q: What is the possession date for Birla Khar West?**\n\nA: No possession date has been officially confirmed. Possession dates are only committed at RERA filing. Based on the project announcement in March 2026 and typical Mumbai redevelopment timelines, a 2029–2031 window is broadly indicative — but this is not confirmed by any official source.\n\n**Q: What is the expected price range for Birla Khar West?**\n\nA: Official pricing has not been disclosed. Based on the ₹1,700 crore revenue target across 2.9 lakh sq.ft, analysts estimate an average selling price of approximately ₹58,600/sq.ft. For the ~1,906 sq.ft 3 BHK, an indicative all-in range of ₹11 Cr to ₹14 Cr+ is plausible — though final RERA-stage pricing may differ meaningfully.\n\n**Q: Is pre-launch booking open? How does it work?**\n\nA: Some channel partners are circulating pre-launch interest registration forms. Be aware: pre-RERA bookings carry no legal protection under RERA. Any amounts paid before RERA registration are at the buyer's risk. Wait for MahaRERA filing before making financial commitments, or at minimum consult a real estate lawyer before signing anything.\n\n**Q: Who is Parinee Real Estate Builders and why is the JV important?**\n\nA: Parinee Real Estate Builders is a Mumbai-based developer with experience specifically in housing society redevelopment — the exact capability Birla Estates needed as a first-time MMR redevelopment entrant. The JV structure means Birla brings brand equity and capital; Parinee brings local regulatory and community-liaison know-how. This complementary structure is a positive signal for execution, though it does not eliminate redevelopment risks entirely.\n\n**Q: What is the nearest metro station to Birla Khar West?**\n\nA: The upcoming Khar Metro Station on Metro Line 2 (Dahisar–Mankhurd) is approximately 0.6 km from the project site. Once operational, it will directly connect residents to BKC, Lower Parel, and eventually Mankhurd. The existing Bandra Metro Station (Line 1, Versova–Andheri–Ghatkopar) is approximately 1.9 km away.\n\n**Q: Is Birla Khar West a good investment?**\n\nA: The location is genuinely strong — Khar West has delivered 16.4% YoY price appreciation and enjoys near-zero new land supply. The metro upside is real. The risks are equally real: pre-RERA status, first-time MMR redevelopment execution for Birla Estates, and pricing that will likely push all-in costs to ₹15 Cr+ for prime units. Investors with a 5-year horizon and risk tolerance for pre-RERA exposure may find value; those wanting certainty should wait for RERA registration.\n\n**Q: How does Birla Khar West compare to Rustomjee Paramount?**\n\nA: Rustomjee Paramount is a delivered, RERA-registered product in Khar West currently trading at ~₹74,100/sq.ft — it has a proven OC and occupancy track record. Birla Khar West is a pre-RERA new launch where you are buying on location merit and brand promise. Buyers who value certainty should factor in the risk-reward trade-off carefully. Those betting on launch-to-delivery appreciation and the Birla brand premium may find Khar West a compelling entry point at final RERA pricing — but comparison at this stage is premature since final Birla pricing has not been announced.\n\n## Related News\n\n* [Birla Estates Enters Mumbai Redevelopment Market With ₹1,700 Crore Luxury Project In Khar West](/news/birla-estates-enters-mumbai-redevelopment-market-with-1700-crore-luxury-project-in-khar-west.html)\n\n### Questions & Answers (0)\n\nPopular:\n\nPreparing your answer…\n\n🔒 Unlock your full answer\n\nWe’ll show it here and send a copy to your WhatsApp.\n\n### Terms & Conditions — Q&A\n\nBy submitting a question on RealtyPromoo, you agree to these terms:\n\n#### 1. Content Policy\n\n* Your question must be a genuine real estate query.\n* No abusive, defamatory, or promotional content.\n* No personal contact info, broker referrals, or spam.\n* Questions are reviewed by AI and may be edited for clarity, grammar, or politeness before publication.\n\n#### 2. Publication\n\n* Your first name + last initial (e.g., \"Rahul S.\") will be displayed publicly with the answer.\n* Your full name, phone number, and email are **never** displayed publicly.\n* Once published, your question and answer become part of RealtyPromoo's content.\n\n#### 3. Phone & Email\n\n* Your phone number is required so our team can share the answer with you on WhatsApp and assist with your query.\n* Your phone number and email are stored securely and may be used by RealtyPromoo or its sales team to contact you regarding your query or related properties.\n\n#### 4. Answer Accuracy\n\n* Answers are generated by AI based on publicly available information and the page context.\n* Answers are informational only — not financial, legal, or investment advice.\n* Always verify pricing, RERA status, and possession dates with the developer before any transaction.\n* RealtyPromoo is not