l-developers-partners-with-japans-marubeni-corporation-for-fifth-india-real-estate-development-project-in-pune)\n\nMarubeni Corporation partners with Kolte-Patil Developers for fifth India project in Pune's Life Republic. 1.1M sq ft, 900 homes, ₹850 crore GDV. Launch...\n\n[![Blackstone Invests $378 Million In South City Mall Kolkata, Largest Commercial Real Estate Deal Of Q1 2026](/images/news/blackstone-invests-378-million-in-south-city-mall-kolkata-largest-commercial-rea.webp) News](/news/blackstone-invests-378-million-in-south-city-mall-kolkata-largest-commercial-real-estate-deal-of-q1-2026) \n\n### [Blackstone Invests $378 Million In South City Mall Kolkata, Largest Commercial Real Estate Deal Of Q1 2026](/news/blackstone-invests-378-million-in-south-city-mall-kolkata-largest-commercial-real-estate-deal-of-q1-2026)\n\nBlackstone acquires South City Mall Kolkata for $378 million in largest Q1 2026 commercial real estate deal. Impact on buyers, market analysis, and what's next.\n\n[![India's Q1 2026 Real Estate Deal Activity Falls 36% In Value To $763 Million Despite 14% Rise In Deal Volumes: Grant Thornton Report](/images/news/india-s-q1-2026-real-estate-deal-activity-falls-36-in-value-to-763-million-despi.webp) News](/news/indias-q1-2026-real-estate-deal-activity-falls-36-in-value-to-763-million-despite-14-rise-in-deal-volumes-grant-thornton-report) \n\n### [India's Q1 2026 Real Estate Deal Activity Falls 36% In Value To $763 Million Despite 14% Rise In Deal Volumes: Grant Thornton Report](/news/indias-q1-2026-real-estate-deal-activity-falls-36-in-value-to-763-million-despite-14-rise-in-deal-volumes-grant-thornton-report)\n\nGrant Thornton Q1 2026 report: India real estate deal values dropped 36% YoY to $763M, with deal volumes up 14%. Commercial assets dominate as investors adopt...\n\n[![RERA 2.0 Launched In March 2026 To Transform Indian Real Estate Transparency](/images/news/rera-2-0-launched-in-march-2026-to-transform-indian-real-estate-transparency-2.webp) News](/news/rera-20-launched-in-march-2026-to-transform-indian-real-estate-transparency) \n\n### [RERA 2.0 Launched In March 2026 To Transform Indian Real Estate Transparency](/news/rera-20-launched-in-march-2026-to-transform-indian-real-estate-transparency)\n\nRERA 2.0 launched March 2026 with third-party audits, digital dashboards, faster dispute resolution (60 days), and expanded project coverage. What homebuyers...\n\n[![Maha Govt Freezes Ready Reckoner Rates For 2026–27, Offering Relief To Real Estate Sector](/images/news/maha-govt-freezes-ready-reckoner-rates-for-2026-27-offering-relief-to-real-estat.webp) News](/news/maha-govt-freezes-ready-reckoner-rates-for-202627-offering-relief-to-real-estate-sector) \n\n### [Maha Govt Freezes Ready Reckoner Rates For 2026–27, Offering Relief To Real Estate Sector](/news/maha-govt-freezes-ready-reckoner-rates-for-202627-offering-relief-to-real-estate-sector)\n\nMaharashtra government freezes Ready Reckoner rates for FY 2026-27. Learn how this 0% hike impacts homebuyers, stamp duty costs, and property prices.\n\n[![Real Estate Developers Acquire 3,093 Acres Of Land In 2025 Investing ₹54,818 Crore](/images/news/real-estate-developers-acquire-3-093-acres-of-land-in-2025-investing-54-818-cror.webp) News](/news/real-estate-developers-acquire-3093-acres-of-land-in-2025-investing-54818-crore) \n\n### [Real Estate Developers Acquire 3,093 Acres Of Land In 2025 Investing ₹54,818 Crore](/news/real-estate-developers-acquire-3093-acres-of-land-in-2025-investing-54818-crore)\n\nDevelopers acquired 3,093 acres for ₹54,818 crore in 2025. Discover how this ₹92,000 crore construction boom will impact property prices and homebuyer...\n\n[![India's Real Estate Attracts $1.2 Billion In Private Equity In Q1 2026](/images/news/india-s-real-estate-attracts-1-2-billion-in-private-equity-in-q1-2026.webp) News](/news/indias-real-estate-attracts-12-billion-in-private-equity-in-q1-2026) \n\n### [India's Real Estate Attracts $1.2 Billion In Private Equity In Q1 2026](/news/indias-real-estate-attracts-12-billion-in-private-equity-in-q1-2026)\n\nIndia's real estate sector secured $1.2 billion in private equity in Q1 2026. Discover how this commercial boom impacts homebuyers and property prices.\n\n[![Birla Estates Enters Mumbai Redevelopment Market With ₹1,700 Crore Luxury Project In Khar West](/images/news/birla-estates-enters-mumbai-redevelopment-market-with-1-700-crore-luxury-project.webp) News](/news/birla-estates-enters-mumbai-redevelopment-market-with-1700-crore-luxury-project-in-khar-west) \n\n### [Birla Estates Enters Mumbai Redevelopment Market With ₹1,700 Crore Luxury Project In Khar West](/news/birla-estates-enters-mumbai-redevelopment-market-with-1700-crore-luxury-project-in-khar-west)\n\nBirla Estates debuts in Mumbai's redevelopment market with a ₹1,700 crore luxury project in Khar West. Discover the impact on homebuyers and property prices.\n\n[![Birla Estates Partners With Sikka Group To Develop ₹1,600 Crore Residential Project In Greater Noida Under Up Legacy Revival Policy](/images/news/birla-estates-partners-with-sikka-group-to-develop-1-600-crore-residential-proje.webp) News](/news/birla-estates-partners-with-sikka-group-to-develop-1600-crore-residential-project-in-greater-noida-under-up-legacy-revival-policy) \n\n### [Birla Estates Partners With Sikka Group To Develop ₹1,600 Crore Residential Project In Greater Noida Under Up Legacy Revival Policy](/news/birla-estates-partners-with-sikka-group-to-develop-1600-crore-residential-project-in-greater-noida-under-up-legacy-revival-policy)\n\nBirla Estates invests ₹500 crore with Sikka Group for ₹1,600 crore Greater Noida revival project. UP Legacy Policy enables stalled housing comeback. Launch...\n\n[![Hyderabad Real Estate's Sharp Slowdown: Why New Home Launches Crashed 46% In Q1 2026 And What Buyers Should Do Next](/images/news/hyderabad-real-estate-s-sharp-slowdown-why-new-home-launches-crashed-46-in-q1-20.webp) News](/news/hyderabad-real-estates-sharp-slowdown-why-new-home-launches-crashed-46-in-q1-2026-and-what-buyers-should-do-next) \n\n### [Hyderabad Real Estate's Sharp Slowdown: Why New Home Launches Crashed 46% In Q1 2026 And What Buyers Should Do Next](/news/hyderabad-real-estates-sharp-slowdown-why-new-home-launches-crashed-46-in-q1-2026-and-what-buyers-should-do-next)\n\nHyderabad recorded a 46% year-on-year crash in new home launches in Q1 2026, with zero launches in March. Here's what drove it, which areas still offer...\n\n[![India's Real Estate Market Enters a New Era of Divergence: Q1 2026 Data Reveals a Split Nation](/images/news/share-on-x.webp) Market Update](/news/indias-real-estate-market-enters-a-new-era-of-divergence-q1-2026-data-reveals-a-split-nation) \n\n### [India's Real Estate Market Enters a New Era of Divergence: Q1 2026 Data Reveals a Split Nation](/news/indias-real-estate-market-enters-a-new-era-of-divergence-q1-2026-data-reveals-a-split-nation)\n\nIndia's Q1 2026 property market shows sharp city-level divergence. PE investment hits $1.2B, Bengaluru and Chennai surge while Hyderabad launches crash 46%...\n\n## EXPRESS YOUR INTEREST\n\n ","images":[]},{"url":"https://birlaestatesltd.com/localities/malabar-hill","title":"Birla Estates at Walkeshwar, Malabar Hill Mumbai | Birla Anayu","raw_content":"![Birla Estates](/media/branding/logo-site-logo-k08cxq.webp)\n\n# Birla Estates projects in Walkeshwar, Malabar Hill, Mumbai\n\n## Birla Estates in South Mumbai's Most Constrained Address\n\nAditya Birla Group entered real estate in 2016 through Aditya Birla Real Estate Limited — formerly Century Textiles and Industries Limited — which is the holding company of Birla Estates Private Limited. That is a relatively recent entry for a conglomerate whose founding entity dates to 1897, which makes the choice of Walkeshwar, Malabar Hill as one of its first Mumbai residential addresses a deliberate signal about where the developer intends to anchor its reputation in the city.\n\nSince its founding in 2016, Birla Estates has provided homes to over 3,100 families and developed nearly 30 million square feet of space, with an additional 9.3 million square feet currently under construction. Between FY20 and FY25, Birla Estates recorded a 77% compound annual growth rate in residential booking value. That trajectory matters to a Malabar Hill buyer because it indicates an operator who is scaling — not a boutique studio that may lack delivery infrastructure on an ultra-luxury project of this complexity.\n\nThe business has a well-established commercial portfolio with two Grade-A commercial buildings located in Worli, Mumbai, with approximately six lakh square feet of leasable area, alongside a residential portfolio of multiple projects with area under development exceeding ten lakh square metres. Worli and Malabar Hill share the South Mumbai geography; the developer's existing footprint at Century Bhavan and Birla Niyaara (Worli) means Birla Estates already operates build-and-manage infrastructure in the same coastal belt where Birla Anayu sits.\n\n## Birla Anayu: What the Project Actually Is\n\nBirla Anayu is a sea-facing residential building on Walkeshwar Road in Malabar Hill. The structure is designed around a single-residence-per-floor format — a configuration that is architecturally and commercially unusual even for Malabar Hill. Each sprawling residence commands an entire floor, crafted to frame extraordinary bay views.\n\nBirla Anayu offers 4 BHK and Duplex apartments with pricing starting at ₹70 crore, with carpet areas ranging from 4,000 to 7,000 sq ft. Each floor boasts a single apartment with a 3,919 sq ft carpet area and a private entrance lobby. The floor-to-floor height is 13.8 feet.\n\nResidents can indulge in 270-degree panoramic views of the Arabian Sea from expansive decks, and the first residential unit begins at 25 metres above ground level, ensuring unobstructed sea views. The site is situated on Walkeshwar Main Road, just 400 metres from the Jain Temple.\n\nEvery apartment includes an exclusive multi-usage parking floor, with each unit receiving an entire floor dedicated to parking. Birla Anayu is designed with 100% Vastu compliance, with customizable layouts that allow residents to tailor their living spaces.\n\nThe project is registered with MahaRERA under Project Registration No. P51900077140, verifiable at maharera.mahaonline.gov.in. Birla Anayu was launched in August 2020 and is expected to be ready by March 2029.\n\n## Amenities and Interior Specification\n\nThe 17th floor features an infinity pool, gym, entertainment deck, and lounge, providing the setting for relaxation and social gatherings. The project offers amenities including a rooftop infinity pool, sundecks, a floating restaurant near the swimming pool, musical walkways, shallow brooks, a maze garden, a sculpture garden, smart home automation, a yoga lawn, reflexology path, a pet-friendly area, and modern elevators.\n\nInteriors include branded fixtures and fittings, marble floors, and oak timber furnishings. The multi-level security mechanism features vigilance security personnel and CCTV cameras, with intercom systems at the perimeter and entry registers that record the arrival and departure of every visitor and staff member, including vehicle details.\n\nBirla Estates prioritises an eco-friendly living environment, with sustainable initiatives including rainwater harvesting, waste management measures, and energy-saving methods.\n\n## Why Walkeshwar Commands These Prices — and Why That Supports a Birla Estates Buyer\n\nUnderstanding what a buyer gets from the location is inseparable from understanding what Birla Estates gains by building here. Walkeshwar is not simply a postcode; it is a micromarket with hard supply constraints.\n\nProperty rates in Malabar Hill have shown a clear upward trajectory, moving from ₹61,050 per sq ft in June 2025 to ₹95,700 per sq ft by March 2026. This consistent growth highlights the sustained demand for premium real estate in this exclusive pocket of South Mumbai, and the significant jump in rates reflects the narrowing supply of high-end residential inventory.\n\nWalkeshwar itself offers apartments at an average price of ₹87,350 per sq ft, with a 15% year-on-year change in apartment prices. Walkeshwar leads the rental market within the Malabar Hill belt with rates of ₹250 per sq ft, showing a strong growth of 18.95%. For a buyer at Birla Anayu, the rental yield backdrop is as relevant as the capital appreciation story.\n\nKey landmarks in Malabar Hill include the Hanging Gardens, Pherozeshah Mehta Gardens, the Banganga Tank — one of the oldest water tanks in Mumbai — the Raj Bhavan (official residence of the Governor of Maharashtra), and the Walkeshwar Temple complex. These are not changeable. The cultural and civic density of this small peninsular hill is fixed by geography and history, which is precisely why supply of developable land is so limited.\n\n## Connectivity: Getting In and Out of the Hill\n\nThe residential project is seamlessly connected to the other parts of the city through Napean Sea Road. Malabar Hill is connected to major roads including Marine Drive, Pedder Road, and the Western Express Highway, enabling easy access to different parts of the city.\n\nCharni Road and Marine Lines are the closest train stations, offering access for residents of Birla Anayu. Residents enjoy easy access to key business districts such as Nariman Point and Lower Parel. For those commuting to the Bandra-Kurla Complex, the Bandra-Worli Sea Link — reachable via Marine Drive and Worli — makes that corridor usable without traversing central Mumbai's inner roads.\n\n## Social Infrastructure Within Reach\n\n## Birla Estates' Broader Mumbai Footprint\n\nBirla Anayu at Walkeshwar sits at the ultra-luxury end of a Mumbai portfolio that spans multiple price points and geographies. Birla Niyaara in Worli is a lavish apartment complex spread over 10 acres, offering a range of 2 to 7 BHK apartments, scheduled for completion in 2028. Birla Vanya in Thane covers 21 acres with 1 to 3 BHK flats. Birla Century Mills in Worli, South Mumbai, offers 2 BHK, 2.5 BHK, and 3 BHK apartments.\n\nThis range tells a buyer at Birla Anayu something concrete: Birla Estates operates simultaneously at the township scale (Birla Vanya, Birla Niyaara) and the ultra-boutique scale (Birla Anayu's reported eight units), which means the developer does not rely on any single product type for its financial continuity. The Walkeshwar project is not carrying the developer's cashflow — it is a statement of positioning at the top of the South Mumbai market.\n\n## Frequently Asked *Questions*\n\nInformation on this site is for general reference and does not constitute an offer. Prices are subject to change without notice and properties are subject to availability. Images are for representation only. This is not the official website of Birla Estates. It is operated by a RERA-registered marketing partner.","images":[]},{"url":"https://keystonerealestateadvisory.com/buy/new/birla-anayu-project-malabar-hill-mumbai/1309","title":"Birla Anayu Malabar Hill | Latest Price, Floor Plans & Brochure","raw_content":"![](https://www.facebook.com/tr?id=1944469116304081&ev=PageView&noscript=1)\n![](https://www.facebook.com/tr?id=2462545180935377&ev=PageView&noscript=1)\n![keystonerealestateadvisory.com](https://keystonerealestateadvisory.com/public/img/gallery/ks-logo.webp)\n![Birla Anayu Amenity 1](https://keystonerealestateadvisory.com/public/uploads/property/HPk9pqmP4CPlAi4MuGUYJEOkKt10g3iEj7yTBYkM.webp)\n![Birla Anayu Project Images 2](https://keystonerealestateadvisory.com/public/uploads/property/48b3gwBzHcFFsLzC8cI09QzZa0l7Ekk0dWABAcyU.webp)\n\n## About Birla Anayu\n\n### Overview\n\n![Project Area](https://keystonerealestateadvisory.com/public/img/network.svg)\n![ Number of Storey's](https://keystonerealestateadvisory.com/public/img/building.svg)\n![Parking Type](https://keystonerealestateadvisory.com/public/img/construction.svg)\n![Possession Date](https://keystonerealestateadvisory.com/public/img/calendar.svg)\n![Possession Status](https://keystonerealestateadvisory.com/public/img/construction.svg)\n![ Number of Storey's](https://keystonerealestateadvisory.com/public/img/building.svg)\n\n### Key Highlights\n\n* **Savor 270-degree wide views of the sea**\n* **Only 1 apartment per floor with a private lobby**\n* **Dedicated parking space for each apartment**\n\n**Savor 270-degree wide views of the sea**\n\n**Only 1 apartment per floor with a private lobby**\n\n**Dedicated parking space for each apartment**\n\n### Introduction\n\nBirla Anayu Project Overview  \nFor a Birla Estates project, Call Us Today! And for Birla Anayu project details, check out the description below.\n\nBirla Anayu Address  \nLocated in Malabar Hill, Mumbai, Birla Anayu by Birla Estates offers ultra-premium 4BHK residences with exceptional privacy, sea views, and world-class lifestyle comforts.\n\nProject Details  \n• Birla Anayu is spread across 0.19 acres with G+15 storeys designed as exclusive ultra-luxury residences.  \n• Birla Anayu offers expansive 4BHK apartments, each occupying an entire floor with a private lobby for unmatched exclusivity.  \n• The premium development includes high-end lifestyle amenities such as a clubhouse, swimming pool, yoga zone, gym, and jogging track.  \n• Birla Anayu ensures complete comfort with airy rooms, power backup, 24\\*7 water supply, parking, lift access, and advanced security systems.  \n• Located in the prestigious Malabar Hill area, the project provides stunning 270-degree sea views and seamless access to Marine Drive, Walkeshwar, and key South Mumbai landmarks.\n\nCarpet Area  \nBirla Anayu carpet area details are given below:  \n4BHK – 3914 sq.ft.\n\nLifestyle Amenities  \nClub House  \nJogging Track  \nKids Play Area  \nSwimming Pool  \nYoga Zone  \nGym\n\nFacilities  \nIntercom  \nLift  \nPower Back Up  \nParking  \nSecurity System  \nAiry Rooms  \n24\\*7 Water\n\nWhy to Invest in this Property?  \n• One of South Mumbai’s most prestigious luxury addresses.  \n• Exclusive single-apartment-per-floor residences with private lobbies.  \n• 270-degree Arabian Sea views offering unmatched visual luxury.  \n• Ultra-premium amenities ideal for elite lifestyle seekers.  \n• Strong appreciation potential in one of Mumbai’s highest-value micro-markets.\n\nPossession & RERA  \nExpected possession: March 2029  \nMahaRERA registration number: P51900077140\n\n### Download Brochure\n\n## Pricing of Birla Anayu\n\n### Pricing & Unit Plans\n\n![4 BHK  Unit Plan](https://keystonerealestateadvisory.com/public/img/layout.webp)\n\n## Property Features of Birla Anayu\n\n### Amenities\n\n![Club house](https://keystonerealestateadvisory.com/public/uploads/amenity/XHmlGOsa5pmWAop1jsrzbhwfyh0ZziFBsDDydKHm.webp)\n![Jogging Track](https://keystonerealestateadvisory.com/public/uploads/amenity/0MdcVu1dWQscKGxYPlOEvfKZG17sbpLwkkWHGQus.webp)\n![Kids Play Area](https://keystonerealestateadvisory.com/public/uploads/amenity/caC1nd4EG3aPxrSHSy42KOuI69993uXqnhmO5wM1.webp)\n![Swimming Pool](https://keystonerealestateadvisory.com/public/uploads/amenity/SFZjCUNkC7Mx0X3VU5OrVgx4mtJUvqfykBy0PZer.webp)\n![Yoga Zone](https://keystonerealestateadvisory.com/public/uploads/amenity/COwM5RjENyf7U7nEW3taZHaXwLNwUKHFpeE88skI.webp)\n![Gym](https://keystonerealestateadvisory.com/public/uploads/amenity/IGXHlscIm9ZRf5Dwqaa7fOuHpxoQXC8VN6qHvSos.webp)\n\n### Facilities\n\n![Intercom](https://keystonerealestateadvisory.com/public/uploads/amenity/CBrT8D2Yj9H3yZtjvMxDM3OAtAQg0yw7lKqZpr8h.webp)\n![Lift](https://keystonerealestateadvisory.com/public/uploads/amenity/PlsX6Ye4mz30wZTyU2HUzRfZZAF1UyAfAPcv7UW6.webp)\n![Power Back Up](https://keystonerealestateadvisory.com/public/uploads/amenity/hyhD5ZsEryAKGW3ZBDuJfwfIbR00KY59KGRA3TdM.webp)\n![Parking](https://keystonerealestateadvisory.com/public/uploads/amenity/Mn1Br3z95nMIVacp1Oa7MFHiuII6ZjpgFaetLKCL.webp)\n![Security System](https://keystonerealestateadvisory.com/public/uploads/amenity/6dsfc7xPvlsYjnrmZXSMQCe0h9jTiIuqmb3G3wvM.webp)\n![Airy Rooms](https://keystonerealestateadvisory.com/public/uploads/amenity/T45jLRY6wMGBiz3hvUPuSsYeNtObK7CQdWXudLRh.webp)\n![24*7 Water](https://keystonerealestateadvisory.com/public/uploads/amenity/8r8bjKftbO1sSY8rBawv8AexZBpGB5Yes5BaCx4g.png)\n![No open drainage around](https://keystonerealestateadvisory.com/public/uploads/amenity/rEgq45Ei79dPeWZ8gqdrkaHlp6TBQvwjWi8VpCVR.webp)\n![Gated Society](https://keystonerealestateadvisory.com/public/uploads/amenity/dDrSaKbMFrQab5ychFhoq4q88iDVDHgsAU0z9gxn.webp)\n\n## Bank Offers\n\n![About Keystone Real Estate Advisory](https://keystonerealestateadvisory.com/public/ks/images/home-loan-banner.webp)\n![Aditya Birla Capital](https://keystonerealestateadvisory.com/public/uploads/banklogos/XGrM42hFHDybp1Y19862M4OyJ8gDOsg3EE9GTEB1.webp)\n![Axis Bank Home Loan](https://keystonerealestateadvisory.com/public/uploads/banklogos/QZdtxvhynBtBOc30oXZBnWVc5XQBY2AurKebGOt2.webp)\n![Bajaj Finserv](https://keystonerealestateadvisory.com/public/uploads/banklogos/AXQcBE3UdCXzDqCrUfdYix4bnsRarkLpNFpY10H8.webp)\n![Bank of Baroda](https://keystonerealestateadvisory.com/public/uploads/banklogos/6MLWA1aTbSguKjxxqZVVnPer7FyazH85YXJv5wKD.webp)\n![Citi Bank](https://keystonerealestateadvisory.com/public/uploads/banklogos/LHciFR3ExZu3X7BihADb9fpp2Z3Di0ilFvyjptMj.webp)\n![HDFC Home Loans](https://keystonerealestateadvisory.com/public/uploads/banklogos/k3SCEAb5zwzavNb1Y4gZHIIQ3BcUHxpxXR91uXrP.webp)\n![ICICI Bank](https://keystonerealestateadvisory.com/public/uploads/banklogos/dqWrCKj6YqYmSpdnc40KNaPQPIv9Bf22dDHhDJiq.webp)\n![LIC Housing Finanace](https://keystonerealestateadvisory.com/public/uploads/banklogos/ka0moGXIt4v3z8y16KQ8ruJG3F4rd40bQOManwKw.webp)\n![PNB Housing](https://keystonerealestateadvisory.com/public/uploads/banklogos/6qI41xrrVMUFAEQxiGmSUiVbE48cfvqF8GTHp9CE.webp)\n![SBI Home Loans](https://keystonerealestateadvisory.com/public/uploads/banklogos/6LuvpQu1AjCfFOMusgBFDVfK8REKUqT5rwwi9psG.webp)\n\n## Location of Birla Anayu\n\n### Google Map\n\n### Location AV\n\n### About Malabar Hill\n\nThe most exclusive and expensive residential address in India, Malabar Hill is home to top politicians, industrialists, and celebrities. It offers panoramic views of the Back Bay and the Queen’s Necklace. Highlights include the Hanging Gardens, the Kamala Nehru Park, and the historic Banganga Tank. It is a quiet, leafy, and highly secure enclave that represents the pinnacle of Mumbai’s social and financial hierarchy.\n\n**Malabar Hill Location Offers Proximity To:**\n\n* Charni Road\n* Grant Road\n* Maheshwari Devi Temple\n* Mumbai Central\n* Marine Lines Railway station\n* Malbar Hill Police Station Bus Stop\n\n**Popular Landmarks in Malabar Hill**\n\n* Sardar Pav Bhaji\n* Haji Ali Juice Centre\n* Shalimar Restaurant\n* Sukh Sagar\n* Pizza By The Bay\n\n**Schools and Colleges in Malabar Hill**\n\n* Walsingham House School\n* ORCHIDS The International School - CBSE School in Masjid\n* Aditya Birla World Academy\n* Villa Theresa High School\n* Bhavans College\n\n**Hospitals in Malabar Hill**\n\n* Sir H. N. Reliance Foundation Hospital and Research Centre\n* Jaslok Hospital & Research Centre\n* Narayana Health SRCC Children's Hospital\n* Wockhardt Hospitals, Mumbai Central\n* Dr. Manish S Shah Clinic | Unit of Dr Agarwals Eye Hospital\n\n**Shopping and Entertainment in Malabar Hill**\n\n* CR2 Shopping Mall\n* City Centre Mumbai\n* Rubberwala The Platinum Mall\n* Bharat Bazar Mall\n\nThe most exclusive and expensive residential address in India, Malabar Hill is home to top politicians, industrialists, and celebrities. It offers panoramic views of the Back Bay and the Queen’s Necklace. Highlights include the Hanging Gardens, the Kamala Nehru Park, and the historic Banganga Tank. It is a quiet, leafy, and highly secure enclave that represents the pinnacle of Mumbai’s social and finan